import{_ as t,o as a,c as r,ae as o}from"./chunks/framework.BvHJbMD4.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The Tragic Fate of the Alsberg Family – The Human Cost of \\"Aryanization\\" and Helmut Horten's Role","description":"An in-depth research on the Jewish entrepreneurial family Alsberg, their department stores, the brutal \\"Aryanization\\" by the Nazis, and the individual suffering of its members.","frontmatter":{"title":"The Tragic Fate of the Alsberg Family – The Human Cost of \\"Aryanization\\" and Helmut Horten's Role","description":"An in-depth research on the Jewish entrepreneurial family Alsberg, their department stores, the brutal \\"Aryanization\\" by the Nazis, and the individual suffering of its members."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/recherche/alsberg-brueder.md","filePath":"en/recherche/alsberg-brueder.md"}`),i={name:"en/recherche/alsberg-brueder.md"};function n(s,e,h,l,d,u){return a(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="the-tragic-fate-of-the-alsberg-family-–-the-human-cost-of-aryanization-and-helmut-horten-s-role" tabindex="-1">The Tragic Fate of the Alsberg Family – The Human Cost of &quot;Aryanization&quot; and Helmut Horten&#39;s Role <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-tragic-fate-of-the-alsberg-family-–-the-human-cost-of-aryanization-and-helmut-horten-s-role" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Tragic Fate of the Alsberg Family – The Human Cost of &quot;Aryanization&quot; and Helmut Horten&#39;s Role&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The story of the Alsberg family and their once flourishing department store empire is a harrowing testimony to the crimes of National Socialism and the systematic destruction of Jewish life and entrepreneurship in Germany. It exemplarily illustrates the foundation of injustice and human suffering upon which the wealth of some profiteers of the Nazi era, such as Helmut Horten, was built.</p><h2 id="the-roots-of-a-retail-giant-the-alsberg-family-and-gebruder-alsberg-ag" tabindex="-1">The Roots of a Retail Giant: The Alsberg Family and &quot;Gebrüder Alsberg AG&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-roots-of-a-retail-giant-the-alsberg-family-and-gebruder-alsberg-ag" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Roots of a Retail Giant: The Alsberg Family and &quot;Gebrüder Alsberg AG&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The family history began with <strong>Salomon Alsberg</strong>. His son <strong>Siegfried Alsberg (1850–1935)</strong> became the visionary founder of one of the most important department store groups in the German Reich: &quot;Gebrüder Alsberg AG&quot;, headquartered in Cologne. Under his leadership, the company grew into a flourishing empire with locations in Bochum, Duisburg, Neuss, Gelsenkirchen, Dresden, and many other cities.</p><h2 id="aryanization-systematic-expropriation" tabindex="-1">&quot;Aryanization&quot;: Systematic Expropriation <a class="header-anchor" href="#aryanization-systematic-expropriation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;&quot;Aryanization&quot;: Systematic Expropriation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>With the Nazi seizure of power in 1933, a process of persecution and expropriation began, euphemistically called &quot;Aryanization&quot;. Jewish business owners were pressured to sell their companies far below value.</p><h3 id="the-duisburg-example-and-helmut-horten-s-role" tabindex="-1">The Duisburg Example and Helmut Horten&#39;s Role <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-duisburg-example-and-helmut-horten-s-role" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Duisburg Example and Helmut Horten&#39;s Role&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A particularly prominent example concerns the Alsberg store in <strong>Duisburg</strong>. On <strong>May 1, 1936</strong>, the then only 26-year-old <strong>Helmut Horten</strong> took over this significant branch. This transaction took place in the context of massive state pressure and boycotts. Horten, who profited from these policies, laid the foundation for his later empire with this and similar &quot;Aryanizations&quot;. His wealth is thus inextricably linked to the injustice and suffering of the Alsberg family.</p><h2 id="individual-fates-the-human-tragedy" tabindex="-1">Individual Fates: The Human Tragedy <a class="header-anchor" href="#individual-fates-the-human-tragedy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Individual Fates: The Human Tragedy&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The personal suffering went far beyond the loss of their life&#39;s work. It is a story of expulsion, deportation, and murder.</p><ul><li><strong>Siegfried Alsberg</strong> died in 1935. His widow <strong>Emma Alsberg</strong> was deported to Theresienstadt in 1942, where she died at the age of 85.</li><li>Their son <strong>Dr. Alfred Alsberg</strong> was deported to the Litzmannstadt (Łódź) Ghetto, where he starved to death in 1943. His wife <strong>Martha Alsberg</strong> was murdered in the Kulmhof (Chełmno) extermination camp in 1944.</li><li><strong>The Survivors:</strong> Three children, Eva, Fritz, and Heinz Alsberg, managed to flee abroad, some through the Kindertransport to England.</li></ul><hr><p><em>For our mockumentary, this research forms the moral core of Part 3.</em></p>',13)])])}const f=t(i,[["render",n]]);export{g as __pageData,f as default};
